WEBVTT

00:00:10.920 --> 00:00:12.670
<i>The Digimon Encyclopedia!</i>

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.180
<i>Garurumon.</i>

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:17.310
<i>This Digimon evolves from Gabumon.</i>

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.310
LEVEL: CHAMPION

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.980
<i>Garurumon is speedy
and can confuse enemies in battle.</i>

00:00:17.310 --> 00:00:20.980
TYPE: BEAST

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.250
<i>Yamato-san and Garurumon
make a perfect pair!</i>

00:00:20.980 --> 00:00:23.250
SPECIAL MOVE: FOX FIRE

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:25.400
<i>Now, let's check this out!</i>

00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:28.440
<i>The beautiful fur is
firm enough to be a weapon,</i>

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.820
<i>but I wonder if that ever hurts Yamato-san
who sits on top...</i>

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:35.010
<i>Maybe he sits on a special cushion?
I'm curious...</i>

00:00:37.950 --> 00:00:40.510
<i>Which Digimon will it be next time?</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:48.130
<i>Oh Yeah!
Be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:00:43.370 --> 00:00:48.130
<i>Oh Yeah!
tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:54.220
<i>Pass the orbit beyond the sky</i>

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:54.220
<i>oozora kidou wo koero</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:10.980
<i>Can't hold back this rushing speed</i>

00:01:06.020 --> 00:01:10.980
<i>osaekirenai maenomeri na speed</i>

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:15.990
<i>A familiar town turns into a diorama</i>

00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:15.990
<i>minareta machi ga diorama ni naru</i>

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:21.200
<i>Burst through the unclear skies</i>

00:01:16.110 --> 00:01:21.200
<i>futoumei na sora tsukinukerunda</i>

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:26.370
<i>Blow away your worries and discontent</i>

00:01:21.330 --> 00:01:26.370
<i>nayami toka fuman toka futtobashite</i>

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:31.800
<i>Who needs a journey that's by the book</i>

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:31.800
<i>manual doori no tabi nanka irane</i>

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:37.590
<i>Even if you're lost or trembling,
Raise the altitude</i>

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:37.590
<i>mayottemo furuetemo koudo agete</i>

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:42.470
<i>Oh Yeah!
Show off, mess up, stand back up</i>

00:01:37.720 --> 00:01:42.470
<i>Oh Yeah!
ikigatte shikujitte tachiagatte</i>

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.690
<i>The unknown horizon I watch with you</i>

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:47.690
<i>kimi to mitsumeru michi naru chiheisen</i>

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:52.570
<i>Now, be strong, jump on, become the wind</i>

00:01:47.810 --> 00:01:52.570
<i>saa tsuyogatte tobinotte kaze ni natte</i>

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:58.360
<i>Use the sun
That lights tomorrow as a guide</i>

00:01:52.690 --> 00:01:58.360
<i>asu wo terasu taiyou
mejirushi ni shitesa</i>

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:04.200
<i>Fly off to the Glorious World of freedom</i>

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:04.200
<i>tonde ike jiyuu na Glorious World</i>

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:11.060
<i>Just before they rejoined Taichi's team,</i>

00:02:11.060 --> 00:02:15.440
<i>Yamato's team was attacked
by Mammon and Yukidarumon.</i>

00:02:18.840 --> 00:02:24.080
<i>To carry Sora who was attacked
by Yukidarumon to a warm place,</i>

00:02:24.080 --> 00:02:26.810
<i>Joe decided to become the bait.</i>

00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:32.190
<i>With Joe driven into a corner,</i>

00:02:32.190 --> 00:02:35.280
<i>his determination super evolved
Ikkakumon into Zudomon.</i>

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:38.550
<i>And Zudomon defeated Mammon
with that power.</i>

00:02:43.530 --> 00:02:47.910
<i>Sora had also escaped danger
and recovered to her normal state.</i>

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:55.380
<i>Meanwhile, what lay before Taichi's team
beyond the long caves was...</i>

00:03:08.850 --> 00:03:10.230
Isn't this...

00:03:13.150 --> 00:03:15.170
Humans everywhere...

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:17.670
Did we...

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:20.920
Come back...

00:03:21.240 --> 00:03:22.930
to the real world?

00:03:25.990 --> 00:03:29.480
THE JET-BLACK SHADOW INVADES TOKYO

00:03:29.750 --> 00:03:30.920
Wow!

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:33.230
Large buildings everywhere!

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:39.630
The power failure's... over.

00:03:43.430 --> 00:03:46.280
Did the disaster end already?

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.900
Tokyo was saved?!

00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:50.980
But...

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:56.490
We haven't found
the Holy Digimon yet, have we?

00:03:56.490 --> 00:03:58.150
N-No...

00:03:58.150 --> 00:04:01.300
We've really come back!

00:04:02.490 --> 00:04:06.550
Yes! Now, I can take a shower!

00:04:06.950 --> 00:04:11.790
I can change, listen to music,
and even go shopping!

00:04:14.210 --> 00:04:15.560
And food!

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:16.880
Bubble tea!

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.320
Pancakes!

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:19.440
And...

00:04:19.800 --> 00:04:22.950
Burger Jack's Avocado Cheeseburger!

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.010
Huh?

00:04:24.010 --> 00:04:26.220
Avocado Cheeseburger!

00:04:26.220 --> 00:04:27.810
Is it good?

00:04:27.810 --> 00:04:30.200
Palmon, I bet you'll love it too!

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:33.710
NETWORK ERROR

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:33.710
It's no good.

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:35.570
It won't connect.

00:04:35.570 --> 00:04:36.820
Me neither.

00:04:36.820 --> 00:04:39.820
Are the phones
and the internet not fixed yet?

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:41.910
No, I believe the internet was...

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:43.150
Hey, hey!

00:04:44.030 --> 00:04:46.580
Let's all go to Burger Jack together!

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:47.450
Huh?

00:04:47.450 --> 00:04:51.750
"Burger Jack".
It's a foreign, high-end burger shop.

00:04:51.750 --> 00:04:53.850
Erk! I don't have much on me.

00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:58.630
I'm a bit worried about my house,
so why don't we all go home once?

00:04:58.630 --> 00:05:00.550
Oh. Good point.

00:05:00.550 --> 00:05:03.860
I actually want to shower
and change before I go too.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:06.660
Then let's take the subway.

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:09.050
It's one train to Shibuya.

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:14.290
SHIBUYA: TRAIN WILL ARRIVE SOON

00:05:23.320 --> 00:05:25.800
This subway is amazing.

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:28.490
But it's completely dark outside.

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:30.160
I can't see anything.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:33.080
You can't help that, it's a subway.

00:05:33.080 --> 00:05:34.810
How boring.

00:05:37.830 --> 00:05:40.960
How were we able to come back?

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:46.320
Maybe we beat the Digimon that was causing
the disaster without realizing it?

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:50.720
Oh! Maybe Sora-san's side took care of it!

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:10.370
It's the same old Shibuya...

00:06:11.160 --> 00:06:15.500
Once we get home, I gotta introduce you
to my mom and dad, Palmon!

00:06:15.500 --> 00:06:18.210
Is it okay for me to come along?

00:06:18.210 --> 00:06:19.730
Of course!

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:23.230
But wouldn't your family be surprised?

00:06:23.590 --> 00:06:25.420
They should be, but...

00:06:27.470 --> 00:06:30.490
No one else has taken notice at all.

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:33.020
If we just explain, it'll be fine!

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:35.060
Really!

00:06:36.640 --> 00:06:38.710
We have to change trains here.

00:06:39.060 --> 00:06:40.980
I walk home from here.

00:06:40.980 --> 00:06:44.820
You sure are a rich girl,
living in a place like this!

00:06:44.820 --> 00:06:47.200
Then I'll contact you guys later!

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:48.470
Let's go, Palmon!

00:06:48.470 --> 00:06:49.240
Okay.

00:06:50.990 --> 00:06:52.660
See you!

00:06:56.500 --> 00:06:58.460
The subway again?

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:01.230
This time we'll be outside midway,

00:07:01.670 --> 00:07:03.840
so you'll have some scenery.

00:07:04.750 --> 00:07:06.980
How exciting!

00:07:09.930 --> 00:07:13.890
I wonder if Yamato's side is back too.

00:07:13.890 --> 00:07:16.990
Has the disaster really ended?

00:07:20.020 --> 00:07:24.500
I mean, we haven't
done anything yet, have we?

00:07:29.030 --> 00:07:33.010
Umm... Hachiko Square is over here, so...

00:07:34.070 --> 00:07:35.410
This way, Palmon.

00:07:35.410 --> 00:07:36.510
Okay.

00:07:36.910 --> 00:07:39.250
It keeps changing
with all the construction,

00:07:39.250 --> 00:07:42.770
so even a local like me gets lost here.

00:07:44.670 --> 00:07:48.400
This place is like a maze.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:59.310
What was the Holy Digimon after all?

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:01.140
Hmm...

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:38.060
Even with the construction,
we should be able to leave the station!

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:40.290
Hey, Mimi...

00:08:40.290 --> 00:08:43.200
Weren't we just here earlier?

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:44.310
What?

00:08:50.280 --> 00:08:51.780
Palmon...

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:54.370
Hungry, huh?

00:08:54.370 --> 00:08:55.450
Yeah.

00:08:56.530 --> 00:09:01.170
Palmon, your face looks
like an avocado to me right now.

00:09:01.170 --> 00:09:02.330
What?!

00:09:03.410 --> 00:09:04.180
Oh?!

00:09:11.510 --> 00:09:13.040
Hello!

00:09:13.040 --> 00:09:15.720
This place has the food that you like?

00:09:15.720 --> 00:09:16.970
That's right!

00:09:17.850 --> 00:09:19.200
Hello!

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:21.440
For here or to go?

00:09:21.440 --> 00:09:22.440
For here!

00:09:22.440 --> 00:09:26.460
Um, two Avocado Cheeseburger combos!

00:09:26.460 --> 00:09:27.440
For my drink--

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:30.780
Hello! For here or to go?

00:09:30.780 --> 00:09:31.710
What?

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:35.720
Hello! For here or to go?

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:40.330
Hello! For here or to go?

00:09:41.290 --> 00:09:43.200
Hello...

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:47.850
It's weird, isn't it?

00:09:48.170 --> 00:09:50.860
With such a big disaster like that,

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:54.300
everyone's acting like nothing happened.

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:57.470
Taichi!

00:09:58.110 --> 00:10:01.120
When do we get somewhere bright?

00:10:01.720 --> 00:10:03.040
We're almost...

00:10:04.370 --> 00:10:08.370
You're right,
shouldn't we be outside by now?!

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:12.880
<i>The next station is Shibuya.</i>

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:15.280
<i>Please change here for the JR Lines,
Keio Inokashira Line...</i>

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:18.930
This can't be.
We left Shibuya Station earlier!

00:10:18.930 --> 00:10:22.680
What? We're already at your house, Taichi?

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:26.560
Oh!

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:27.810
Oh!

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:33.130
This place is weird!
We can't get out of the station.

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:34.130
Us too!

00:10:34.130 --> 00:10:35.030
What?!

00:10:35.050 --> 00:10:37.030
ENTER PASSWORD

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:39.530
Please connect!

00:10:41.470 --> 00:10:42.220
Oh?

00:10:43.220 --> 00:10:46.140
Um, excuse me.

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:47.790
Yes.

00:10:48.140 --> 00:10:51.040
We're sorry, we cannot break any bills.

00:10:51.040 --> 00:10:52.030
Huh?!

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:54.290
No, we're looking for the exit.

00:10:54.780 --> 00:10:59.120
We're sorry, we cannot break any bills.

00:10:59.120 --> 00:11:00.180
Ta...

00:11:00.570 --> 00:11:01.950
Taichi-san!

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:07.000
Agumon!

00:11:11.790 --> 00:11:14.130
Is that a Digimon?!

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:20.970
Poison Ivy!

00:11:23.970 --> 00:11:25.700
Petit Thunder!

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:27.890
Baby Flame!

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:52.620
Mimi!

00:11:57.960 --> 00:11:59.210
This is endless!

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:04.010
What's going on?!
Why are there Digimon in Tokyo?!

00:12:04.010 --> 00:12:07.600
I don't know!
Maybe they came while we were gone.

00:12:07.600 --> 00:12:09.120
Or else...

00:12:10.060 --> 00:12:13.870
Taichi-san, this is the gate
we went through earlier!

00:12:13.870 --> 00:12:16.130
Jeez, what do we do?!

00:12:16.440 --> 00:12:18.630
We have to find a different way...

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.150
Watch out!

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:29.140
I see.

00:12:31.330 --> 00:12:33.130
We might be able to escape.

00:12:33.130 --> 00:12:35.210
Agumon, help me out!

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:36.150
Okay!

00:12:38.210 --> 00:12:41.720
Agumon Evolution!

00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.290
Greymon!

00:12:57.460 --> 00:12:59.570
Mega Flame!

00:13:15.000 --> 00:13:16.420
Hurray!

00:13:16.420 --> 00:13:18.230
We escaped! Now, we can go ho--

00:13:18.230 --> 00:13:19.360
No.

00:13:19.670 --> 00:13:20.610
Huh?

00:13:30.060 --> 00:13:31.870
What is this?

00:13:35.310 --> 00:13:38.380
This isn't our world.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:43.630
We're still...

00:13:44.150 --> 00:13:46.030
in the Digital World.

00:13:46.910 --> 00:13:50.280
This is a city made from data,
an artificial Tokyo!

00:13:58.670 --> 00:13:59.940
No way!

00:13:59.940 --> 00:14:03.440
And I thought we were finally back!

00:14:03.880 --> 00:14:05.880
Then Tokyo's still...

00:14:06.590 --> 00:14:09.760
Our world is still in danger!

00:14:11.850 --> 00:14:16.600
<i>All highways leading out of Tokyo
are congested with evacuating vehicles.</i>

00:14:17.350 --> 00:14:19.210
<i>Please do not rush to relocate</i>

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:22.440
<i>and act calmly,
following the authorities' directions.</i>

00:14:25.320 --> 00:14:27.820
Hikari, hurry and get ready.

00:14:29.160 --> 00:14:30.950
I'm ready anytime.

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:33.970
Oh! Where were our health insurance cards?

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:38.870
Now where did I put them?

00:14:39.750 --> 00:14:43.230
<i>"Taichi, we'll be at your grandpa's.
Call us when you return. Mom."</i>

00:14:43.250 --> 00:14:46.550
We can't go back yet.

00:14:46.550 --> 00:14:48.240
We're the only ones...

00:14:52.430 --> 00:14:54.220
who can stop this!

00:14:58.600 --> 00:14:59.790
Mimi.

00:14:59.790 --> 00:15:05.400
Once everything's over, treat me to the
Avocado Cheeseburger in your real city.

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:07.320
Palmon...

00:15:07.320 --> 00:15:10.360
Until then, Mimi, let's do our best!

00:15:12.490 --> 00:15:13.370
Okay!

00:15:18.870 --> 00:15:20.420
I'll do it, all right!

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:24.900
I swear I'm gonna eat
that Avocado Cheeseburger with Palmon!

00:15:32.680 --> 00:15:33.640
Palmon!

00:15:33.640 --> 00:15:34.870
Tentomon!

00:15:35.140 --> 00:15:37.560
Palmon Evolution!

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:39.850
Togemon!

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:41.870
Tentomon Evolution!

00:15:41.870 --> 00:15:43.630
Kabuterimon!

00:15:43.750 --> 00:15:45.750
Mega Flame!

00:15:48.530 --> 00:15:50.510
Mega Blaster!

00:15:52.530 --> 00:15:54.910
Prickly Bang-Bang!

00:16:13.300 --> 00:16:15.530
EYESMON

00:16:16.180 --> 00:16:18.680
They all fused and got bigger!

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:41.790
Greymon Super Evolution!

00:16:56.870 --> 00:16:59.470
Metalgreymon!

00:17:00.310 --> 00:17:03.850
Kabuterimon Super Evolution!

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:07.960
Togemon Super Evolution!

00:17:10.320 --> 00:17:11.240
Lilimon!

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:13.300
Atlurkabuterimon!

00:17:16.320 --> 00:17:18.600
Trident Arm!

00:17:38.010 --> 00:17:39.280
Metalgreymon!

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:42.540
Did a building just suddenly appear?

00:17:44.390 --> 00:17:46.500
Horn Buster!

00:17:55.360 --> 00:17:56.910
Atlurkabuterimon!

00:17:57.360 --> 00:17:59.260
Lilimon, be careful!

00:18:00.660 --> 00:18:01.910
Flower Cannon!

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:08.540
Lilimon!

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:10.380
I've got it!

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:12.320
Eyesmon!

00:18:12.840 --> 00:18:15.050
Huh?! A Champion Digimon?

00:18:15.380 --> 00:18:18.930
Eyesmon's body
can be scattered to eat data

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:22.240
and from that data,
Eyesmon can rebuild objects!

00:18:22.240 --> 00:18:26.150
This city was reassembled
and created by Eyesmon as well.

00:18:26.150 --> 00:18:29.170
In other words, it's like a nest!

00:18:29.170 --> 00:18:32.320
You mean that thing copy and pasted
all of Tokyo?!

00:18:32.320 --> 00:18:34.830
Tokyo's data...

00:18:34.830 --> 00:18:36.670
You don't mean...

00:18:43.370 --> 00:18:47.580
That Eyesmon is causing
Tokyo's power failure!

00:19:01.090 --> 00:19:02.950
Shadow Wing!

00:19:06.060 --> 00:19:07.200
That's...

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:11.210
Taichi! What is this place?

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:13.820
Sora! Is that you?

00:19:15.980 --> 00:19:19.720
Um! We won't get in trouble
if we break that, right?!

00:19:21.990 --> 00:19:24.620
Hammer Spark!

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:32.480
Yagami.

00:19:32.840 --> 00:19:34.170
Yamato!

00:19:34.170 --> 00:19:37.070
<i>We'll talk later.
Let's take this guy down!</i>

00:19:45.260 --> 00:19:46.620
Kaiser Nail!

00:19:56.280 --> 00:19:57.130
Not over yet!

00:19:57.130 --> 00:20:00.030
Let's all focus our attacks together!

00:20:00.030 --> 00:20:01.260
All right!

00:20:21.090 --> 00:20:22.280
Giga Storm!

00:20:22.890 --> 00:20:24.320
Kaiser Nail!

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:26.140
Shadow Wing!

00:20:26.140 --> 00:20:27.450
Flower Cannon!

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.440
Hammer Spark!

00:20:29.440 --> 00:20:31.190
Horn Buster!

00:21:05.640 --> 00:21:07.620
The internet's connected!

00:21:08.010 --> 00:21:11.520
The other side...
the real Tokyo's on the third night.

00:21:11.520 --> 00:21:15.270
<i>...police have suppressed the riot...</i>

00:21:15.940 --> 00:21:18.070
The information is in chaos.

00:21:18.070 --> 00:21:19.480
The third night...

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:22.360
It's almost 72 hours!

00:21:22.360 --> 00:21:25.130
So the situation hasn't changed at all!

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:27.450
What do we do?

00:21:27.450 --> 00:21:30.450
We haven't even met the Holy Digimon yet.

00:21:31.450 --> 00:21:33.380
Wait a minute, this is weird!

00:21:33.380 --> 00:21:37.900
I'm receiving our world's live video
at normal speed.

00:21:38.340 --> 00:21:40.590
Can this be...

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:15.620
<i>Why do these held hands</i>

00:22:11.660 --> 00:22:15.620
<i>naze ima kono te to te nigitte</i>

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:18.290
<i>And the warmth exchanged</i>

00:22:15.750 --> 00:22:18.290
<i>tashikameta taion wo</i>

00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:20.750
<i>Make me reminisce now</i>

00:22:18.420 --> 00:22:20.750
<i>natsukashiku omou noka</i>

00:22:22.460 --> 00:22:26.340
<i>Why an abyss dancing with endless rain</i>

00:22:22.460 --> 00:22:26.340
<i>naze samidare no susabu shinen</i>

00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:28.840
<i>The gaze of that smile</i>

00:22:26.470 --> 00:22:28.840
<i>hohoenda sono shisen ni</i>

00:22:28.970 --> 00:22:30.220
<i>Makes me want to cry</i>

00:22:28.970 --> 00:22:30.220
<i>nakitaku naru</i>

00:22:30.350 --> 00:22:33.140
<i>So call me with that voice</i>

00:22:30.350 --> 00:22:33.140
<i>sono koe de boku wo yonde kure</i>

00:22:33.270 --> 00:22:35.310
<i>This weakness I cannot tell others</i>

00:22:33.270 --> 00:22:35.310
<i>dare ni ienu kono yowasa ga</i>

00:22:35.430 --> 00:22:38.400
<i>I realize is my pillar to stand firm</i>

00:22:35.430 --> 00:22:38.400
<i>tsuyoku tatsu tame no jiku dato omoishiru</i>

00:22:38.520 --> 00:22:40.690
<i>Difference is what makes me adore you</i>

00:22:38.520 --> 00:22:40.690
<i>chigau kara itooshiku naru</i>

00:22:40.810 --> 00:22:43.650
<i>I just want to understand you and me</i>

00:22:40.810 --> 00:22:43.650
<i>tada wakaritai kimi to boku wo</i>

00:22:43.780 --> 00:22:45.860
<i>Scars grow the more we live</i>

00:22:43.780 --> 00:22:45.860
<i>ikiru hodo kizu ga fuete iku</i>

00:22:45.990 --> 00:22:49.110
<i>But still we seek the reasons for us</i>

00:22:45.990 --> 00:22:49.110
<i>sore demo sagashiteiru bokura no wake wo</i>

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:51.370
<i>Overlaying them makes us beautiful</i>

00:22:49.240 --> 00:22:51.370
<i>kasanete wa utsukushiku naru</i>

00:22:51.490 --> 00:22:55.290
<i>I want to know now, I want to cry out</i>

00:22:51.490 --> 00:22:55.290
<i>ima wakaritai sakebi dashitai</i>

00:23:01.960 --> 00:23:04.090
<i>By dodging the gigantic eight heads,</i>

00:23:04.210 --> 00:23:08.090
<i>can Taichi and the others strike
the enemy's weakness?!</i>

00:23:08.220 --> 00:23:12.100
<i>Next time on Digimon Adventure:
"The Battle in Tokyo Against Orochimon "</i>

00:23:12.220 --> 00:23:14.850
<i>The adventure continues to a new world.</i>
